    <!--
      See values/colors.xml. Same shape as day, read downwards: the page starts at its darkest and
      opens into the app's ocean blue at the foot, as day starts white and opens into the aqua.

      L* 6.1 -> 10.3 -> 21.0, a 15-point span where the previous ramp had 6.6 and was not readable
      as a gradient at all. sRGB gives no other way to widen it: at these lightnesses the blues top
      out near C* 17, so the deep end is already at 97% of the chroma its hue can hold and every
      further bit of presence has to come out of lightness. The hue rotates the other way from
      day's, out of the near-neutral blue the page is tinted with and into the aqua as it lightens
      (h 261 -> 243 -> 224), so the colour arrives with the light rather than crossing it.

      The centre sits below the midpoint rather than on it, so the dark holds most of the way down
      and the blue is a glow at the foot instead of a wash over the whole page. That also puts the
      crossover with @color/card_background (L* 14) into the bottom third: a card is lighter than
      the page over most of a screen and darker than it only near the foot, where its 6dp elevation
      is what separates it. Hence the black shadow colour above, rather than day's tinted one.
    -->
    <color name="app_gradient_bottom">#FF023843</color>
    <color name="app_gradient_center">#FF021F2B</color>
